A stand-alone '''''Star Wars'' film''' was being developed by [[Lucasfilm]], with [[Kathleen Kennedy]] and [[Kevin Feige]] serving as its producers and [[Michael Waldron]] as screenwriter. The movie was first confirmed by [[Wikipedia:Walt Disney Studios (division)|Walt Disney Studios]] chairman [[Wikipedia:Alan F. Horn|Alan Horn]] on [[September 25]], [[2019]]. By [[2023]], the film had been canceled.

==Development==
{{Quote|We're finally into it in earnest. I mean, I'm writing away. It's a lot of fun. I'm enjoying having the freedom on that to do something that's not necessarily a sequel or anything. It maybe has a little bit less of a &mdash; it just doesn't have a bunch of TV shows and movies that you're servicing on top of it, the way I did with 'Doctor Strange.' So it's nice. It feels like a different exercise.|Michael Waldron on writing the film|<ref name="Variety Waldron Interview">{{WebCite|url=https://variety.com/2022/film/news/doctor-strange-2-spoilers-scarlet-witch-cameos-1235263318|text='Doctor Strange 2' Screenwriter Defends Wanda's Evolution, Talks Cameos and His 'Star Wars' Script|author=Adam B. Vary|date=2022-05-10|work=[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']]|archivedate=20231109182537}}</ref>}}
[[File:Michael_Waldron_and_Kevin_Feige.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Michael Waldron, screenwriter of the film, and Kevin Feige, producer of the film]]
On [[September 25]], [[2019]], [[Wikipedia:The Hollywood Reporter|''The Hollywood Reporter'']] reported that [[Wikipedia:Marvel Studios|Marvel Studios]] chief [[Kevin Feige]] discussed "a foray into the ''[[Star Wars]]'' universe" with [[Lucasfilm]] President [[Kathleen Kennedy]] and [[Wikipedia:Walt Disney Studios (division)|Walt Disney Studios]] chairman [[Wikipedia:Alan F. Horn|Alan Horn]] in the late summer of that same year. In the same report, Horn confirmed that the news regarding the film was true.<ref name="Feige SW">{{WebCite|url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/marvel-s-kevin-feige-developing-star-wars-movie-disney-1243481|text='Star Wars' Shocker: Marvel's Kevin Feige Developing New Movie for Disney (Exclusive)|author=Kim Masters|date=2019-09-25|work=[[Wikipedia:The Hollywood Reporter|''The Hollywood Reporter'']]|archivedate=20231203175657}}</ref> Feige commented on the film on [[November 10]], saying "I love that world and I love the notion of exploring new people and new places in that universe."<ref name="THR Podcast" /> Kennedy later commented during an interview with [[Wikipedia:Los Angeles Times|''Los Angeles Times'']] on [[December 15]] that Feige pitched the idea for the film but that it was still in early stages.<ref name="Early Stages">{{WebCite|url=https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/story/2019-12-15/kathleen-kennedy-lucasfilm-the-last-jedi-the-mandalorian|text=After 'Rise of Skywalker' and Baby Yoda, Kathleen Kennedy's plan for 'Star Wars' and beyond|author=Ryan Faughnder|date=2019-12-15|work=[[Wikipedia:Los Angeles Times|''Los Angeles Times'']]|archivedate=20230925062421}}</ref>

[[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']], on [[January 7]], [[2021]], reported that screenwriter [[Michael Waldron]] had been hired to write the screenplay for the film.<ref name="Deadline Waldron">{{WebCite|url=https://deadline.com/2021/01/loki-michael-waldron-kevin-feiges-star-wars-movie-as-part-of-newoverall-deal-with-disney-1234665495|text='Loki' Exec Producer Michael Waldron Tapped To Write Kevin Feige's 'Star Wars' Movie As Part Of New Deal With Disney|author=Justin Kroll|date=2021-01-07|work=[[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']]|archivedate=20231128150820}}</ref> On [[June 3]], Waldron confirmed the report during an interview with [[Wikipedia:Vanity Fair (magazine)|''Vanity Fair'']].<ref name="Waldron" /> Waldron confirmed he was currently writing the script for the film in an interview on [[May 6]], [[2022]].<ref name="Deadline Waldron Podcast">{{WebCite|url=https://deadline.com/2022/05/doctor-strange-2-loki-season-2-michael-waldron-podcast-1235018532|text='Doctor Strange 2' Scribe Michael Waldron On "Emotional" 'Loki' Season 2, New 'Star Wars' Pic, & Kang The Conqueror's Whereabouts &ndash; Hero Nation Podcast|author=Anthony D'Alessandro; Dominic Patten|date=2022-05-06|work=[[Wikipedia:Deadline Hollywood|''Deadline'']]|archivedate=20230920044906}}</ref> On [[May 10]], Waldron revealed that the film would be a stand-alone project.<ref name="Variety Waldron Interview" />

[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']] reported that the film had been canceled, saying that Kevin Feige was shifting focus to the future of Marvel Studios on [[March 7]], [[2023]].<ref name="Variety Canceled">{{WebCite|url=https://variety.com/2023/film/news/star-wars-kevin-feige-patty-jenkins-movies-shelved-1235545774|text='Star Wars' Shakeup: Kevin Feige and Patty Jenkins Movies Shelved, Taika Waititi Looking to Star in His Own Film (EXCLUSIVE)|author=Adam B. Vary|date=2023-03-07|work=[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']]|archivedate=20231125132422}}</ref> At [[Celebration Europe (2023)|''Star Wars'' Celebration 2023]], in an interview with [[Wikipedia:IGN|''IGN'']], Kathleen Kennedy denied ever having developed a ''Star Wars'' film with Kevin Feige, saying "it's not an abandoned project, it just didn't happen."<ref name="KK Denial">{{OfficialYouTube|channel=@IGN|name=IGN|link=Wikipedia:IGN|video=qz6s7kvuwMc|text=Kathleen Kennedy on the Future of Star Wars &#124; Star Wars Celebration 2023|date=2023-04-07}}</ref> On [[May 4]], [[Wikipedia:Russo Brothers|Anthony and Joe Russo]] claimed that they had early talks to direct Kevin Feige's film.<ref name="Variety Russos">{{WebCite|url=https://variety.com/2023/film/news/russo-brothers-star-wars-movie-kevin-feige-1235603596|text=Russo Brothers: 'There Were Early Conversations' About Joining Kevin Feige's 'Star Wars' Movie|author=Zack Sharf|date=2023-05-04|work=[[Wikipedia:Variety (magazine)|''Variety'']]|archivedate=20230516231124}}</ref> In an interview on [[November 7]], Feige directly confirmed that the film was no longer in development.<ref name="Kevin Fiege etnow">{{Twitter|etnow|status/1722088080965038268|[[Wikipedia:Entertainment Tonight|''Entertainment Tonight'']]|date=2023-11-08|quote=We are talking to Kevin Feige at 'The Marvels' premiere in Las Vegas and all of our questions we answered!! #TheMarvels|archiveurl=https://archive.is/oqkmd}}</ref>

